\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The two compressions. A large effective space is mapped by a linear code into a much smaller fundamental space. Most of the large space is annihilated (null states), yet on a thin set $\Sigma $---low complexity on the left, sparsity on the right---inner products survive. \Cref  {thm:main} is the statement that these are one phenomenon.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
