\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces E14: the handshake saddle in isolation, $L=c\,\varepsilon r+\frac  h2r^2+\frac  q4(\varepsilon ^2+r^2)^2$ with $h=0.05c$, $q=c$. Left: distance from the saddle against steps; gradient descent waits, then grows exponentially; Adam (both values of $c$ coincide) leaves at once. Right: escape time against $\lvert \lambda _-\rvert $ over two and a half decades. Gradient descent takes 1.6--4\% longer than $\qopname  \relax o{log}(1/z_0)/(\eta \lvert \lambda _-\rvert )$ (the excess grows with $\lvert \lambda _-\rvert $, where the discrete-step and quartic corrections matter); Adam takes 58 steps throughout.}}{18}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:handshake}{{8}{18}{E14: the handshake saddle in isolation, $L=c\,\varepsilon r+\frac h2r^2+\frac q4(\varepsilon ^2+r^2)^2$ with $h=0.05c$, $q=c$. Left: distance from the saddle against steps; gradient descent waits, then grows exponentially; Adam (both values of $c$ coincide) leaves at once. Right: escape time against $\abs {\lambda _-}$ over two and a half decades. Gradient descent takes 1.6--4\% longer than $\log (1/z_0)/(\eta \abs {\lambda _-})$ (the excess grows with $\abs {\lambda _-}$, where the discrete-step and quartic corrections matter); Adam takes 58 steps throughout}{figure.8}{}}
