\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\tocsubsection {}{8.3}{E15: superposition removes the critical point}}{20}{subsection.8.3}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces E15: is the legible code a critical point? Starting from E11's legible codes (same seeds, ReLU receiver), each feature is restricted to its strongest coordinate (shared coordinates kept) and all parameters are polished within that support (full batch of 6144, $\sigma =0.1$). Gradient norms, and root-mean-square per entry, in three groups of directions; ranges are over seeds.}}{20}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
