\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\tocsubsection {}{8.4}{E13: how flat is the legible critical point?}}{20}{subsection.8.4}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces E13: the legible critical point ($d=12$, $n=16$, softplus receiver), polished on a fixed batch of 6144 samples with fixed channel noise. Sender gap: $|\qopname  \relax o{tanh}(A_{o\ell }+a_o)-\qopname  \relax o{tanh}(a_o)|$, at most 2. Residual error of the trained receiver on that batch and on fresh noise (\texttt  {e13\_fresh.py}). Gradient norm within the legible subspace and for leaks into empty coordinates. Global $\lambda _{\qopname  \relax m{min}}$ by Lanczos and the weight of its eigenvector on leaks into empty coordinates. Last three columns: for the least saturated empty coordinate, the leak curvature $H_{\varepsilon \varepsilon }$, the envelope (Schur-complement) curvature, and the I-MMSE prediction $-\phi '(a_j)^2\mathrm  {mmse}_\ell /\sigma ^2$ of \cref  {prop:immse} with the fresh-noise error.}}{21}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
